    {
      "claim": "Bayesian view defines a random variable as the result of a completely deterministic process whose outcome is unknown due to missing information",
      "supported": true,
      "evidence_or_problem": "[00:35:40\u201300:36:16] According to Bayesian framework, the random variable is the result of a completely deterministic process whose outcome is unknown to us only because we left some information which determines the outcome of this process."
    },
    {
      "claim": "In the Bayesian framework, randomness is epistemic (due to incomplete information) rather than ontological",
      "supported": true,
      "evidence_or_problem": "[00:38:54\u201300:39:23] So this is why it's stated here, subjective. So different observers may have different ignorance on the same random variable."
